    "body": "## Summary\n- add a complete user-facing wallet top-up flow on the existing Stripe PaymentIntent backend\n- render Stripe Payment Element by loading Stripe.js directly from js.stripe.com so payment-method data never crosses the doFast API\n- support preset/custom PLN amounts, redirect returns, payment status messaging, manual refresh and webhook-aware balance polling\n- keep the signed Stripe webhook as the only authority that credits the wallet\n- expose only `VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` to the web build while keeping Stripe secret/webhook keys server-side\n- wire local and production Docker builds and document the end-to-end top-up flow\n\n## Security / money boundary\nA browser-side `succeeded` result never mutates wallet state. The existing signed `payment_intent.succeeded` webhook remains the sole credit path and the append-only ledger remains authoritative for reconciliation.\n\n## Local configuration\nThe feature is visible even without Stripe configuration and explains what is missing. A real test payment requires local `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, and public `VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` values. Secrets must not be committed.\n\n## Validation\nCI is the merge gate. Do not merge unless API verify, web lint/build, container/runtime smoke and web container health checks pass.",
